# Service layer

`template.service` holds domain types (`Item`) and `@Service` classes. Domain types have no JPA or Jackson annotations.

Services accept and return domain objects. They call the repository and map with `ModelMapper`:

- read: `ItemEntity` → `Item` via `toDomainObject`
- write: `Item` → `ItemEntity` via `toEntity`

Reads return `Optional` or `List`. Writes that change data use `@Transactional` from `jakarta.transaction`.

Reject invalid domain state with a `final` exception in `template.exception`. Keep the message in `public static final String MESSAGE` and format it in the constructor.

```java
@Transactional
public void create(Item item) {
    if (item.getId() != null) {
        throw new ItemIdAlreadySetException(item.getId());
    }
    repository.create(toEntity(item));
}
```

Do not catch repository failures to return null. Let them propagate.
